## 11. Test gate, auto-rollback, notifications

Full design: `i18n/en/docs/proposals/cicd-test-gate.md`. Walkthrough in
`i18n/en/docs/00-quickstart.md` Phase J.

### Active plugins

- Test runner: `${TEST_RUNNER}` (mode: `${TESTKUBE_MODE}`)
- Rollout plugin: `${ROLLOUT_PLUGIN}`
- Notification providers: `${NOTIFICATION_PROVIDERS}`

### Endpoints

- No dashboard — `ROLLOUT_PLUGIN` is controller-only in v0.3.0 (no Argo
  Rollouts dashboard tier). Canary status: `kubectl argo rollouts get
  rollout <name> -n apps` (kubectl plugin) or `kubectl get rollout -n apps`.
- Testkube agent: namespace `testkube` (`kubectl get pods -n testkube`)
- Argo Rollouts controller (only if `ROLLOUT_PLUGIN=argo-rollouts`):
  namespace `argo-rollouts`

### Notification fan-out

Three events fan out to all enabled notification providers via
`scripts/notify-fanout.sh`: `build-failed` (GitHub Actions workflow),
`deploy-succeeded`/`deploy-failed` (manifest-sync CronJob),
`verify-failed` (the `outpost-verify.timer` systemd timer). Configure /
disable channels by editing `NOTIFICATION_PROVIDERS` in `.env`
(comma-separated) and re-running `bash bootstrap.sh`.

| Provider          | Webhook URL var          | Sign secret var (optional)   |
|-------------------|--------------------------|------------------------------|
| dingtalk          | `DINGTALK_WEBHOOK_URL`   | `DINGTALK_SIGN_SECRET`       |
| feishu            | `FEISHU_WEBHOOK_URL`     | `FEISHU_SIGN_SECRET`         |
| wecom             | `WECOM_WEBHOOK_URL`      | (none — protect URL itself)  |
| webhook-generic   | `GENERIC_WEBHOOK_URL`    | `GENERIC_WEBHOOK_BEARER`     |

### Test contract (per application repo)

Drop `outpost.test.yaml` at the repo root:

```yaml
version: 1
runner:
  command: ["sh", "-c", "go test ./..."]   # or pytest, npm test, mvn test, dotnet test
gates:
  pre-deploy:        { timeout: 5m }
  post-deploy-smoke: { enabled: true, image: curlimages/curl:8.10.0,
                       command: ["sh","-c","curl -fsS http://my-app.apps.svc.cluster.local/healthz"],
                       timeout: 30s }
```

Repos without `outpost.test.yaml` (and without `Dockerfile.test`) skip Gate A
cleanly — pipeline still runs.

### Auto-rollback thresholds (locked)

Default `AnalysisTemplate`: `failureLimit: 2`, `consecutiveErrorLimit: 3`,
`successCondition: result == "Passed"` (Job provider) or `result == 200`
(Web HTTP probe).

## 12. Hardening checklist (recommended, not enforced)

- [ ] Add Cloudflare Access (email OTP) in front of `mq.${ROOT_DOMAIN}`,
      `search.${ROOT_DOMAIN}` — no BasicAuth dashboards left to
      supplement in v0.3.0; this is now the only edge-auth surface.
- [ ] Add basic auth or Cloudflare Access in front of `registry.${ROOT_DOMAIN}` if exposing publicly (currently anonymous).
- [ ] Scope `${GITHUB_RUNNER_PAT}` to the minimum (registration-token
      minting only) and revoke/rotate it after the runner is registered
      — it is not needed for day-to-day operation.
- [ ] Keep the GitHub Actions runner group private-repos-only (GitHub
      default) — never route public-repo PRs to a self-hosted runner.
- [ ] Backup `secrets-backup/sealed-secrets-pub.pem` to a password manager.

## 13. Reuse checklist (when onboarding a new project)

See `i18n/en/docs/05-onboard-project.md`. In short:

1. Create a Gitee/GitHub/GitLab repo with a `Dockerfile`
2. `outpost onboard <repo-url>` — registers it in `OUTPOST_REPOS`
   (verify.sh's reconciliation basis) and prints the CI workflow +
   dual-push setup
3. Copy `templates/github/outpost-build.yml` into the app repo's
   `.github/workflows/` (the onboard command offers to do this for you)
4. Set up dual-push (`git remote set-url --add --push origin <url>` for
   both gitee and github) or a gitee→github one-way push-mirror —
   **no webhook to register anywhere**
5. Add `apps/<name>/{deployment,service,ingress,kustomization}.yaml` to
   the manifest repo (`outpost onboard --manifests-dir <path> --lang
   <lang>` scaffolds this)
6. `git push` (both remotes fire with dual-push) and watch
   `outpost logs sync` — `manifest-sync` converges within
   `${MANIFEST_SYNC_INTERVAL}` minutes

